Thanks to Gabor Zelenak, Steve Freehan for suggesting the 'screen' and
'twin' utilities.

'screen' is part of GNU utils and allows toggling between multiple text
windows on a single serial device.

'twin' allows multiple window areas on the same text screen, which would
allow logs and login to coexist on a single device.

Both are GNU/Linux projects but Screen appears to have been ported also on
Tru64 so I'll give that a try.

Stan Horowitz also made a suggestion to use ssh with networking, but
unfortunately that isn't an option for us due to physical security
restrictions. Thanks for the suggestion.



