I have only two short answers, thanks to Daniel Clar and James Sainsbury

the answer was 

>The way I would go if I wasn't doing it diskless is to define another
>runlevel 5 (say) which started the Xserver to query xdm on the 5.1a server.
>and nothing else.
>eg
>/etc/inittab
>	is:5:initdefault:
>	x11:5:respawn:/usr/bin/X11/X :0 -query myserver


It was what I do

