Thanks to: Maria Gilliland, Phil Baldwin, Paul LaMadeleine, Galen Johnson
and the ubiquitous Dr. Thomas Blinn for their responses.

The answer is perform a complete rolling upgrade (with all the reboots) from
V5.1 to V5.1A, then start another rolling upgrade from V5.1A to V5.1B with
patches.

To quote Dr. Tom:

	Step 1:  Upgrade the whole cluster from V5.1 to V5.1A.  Supported,
gets
	you to the starting point for the V5.1B install.

	Step 2:  Upgrade the whole cluster from V5.1A to V5.1B.  Gets you to
the
	desired end point.

	You can't short-cut this.  The only way I know to really shortcut
the
	procedure is to go back to a single member cluster, then you've only
	got one member to upgrade.  But you can't roll a single member, when
	you come down to it, there would be service disruptions.

Regards

Michael

============================================================

Original question:

Hi there,

We have a number of Tru Cluster clusters running V5.1 that we want to
upgrade to V5.1B. I know that it is necessary to do an installupdate to
V5.1A first. My question is: do you have to complete the whole rolling
upgrade (with all its reboots) for V5.1A before starting a complete new
rolling upgrade for V5.1B, or can you perform both installupdates in the
same Install phase?

Regards

Michael


