Thanks to all who responded. All of you said the same thing which, as I
had suspected, is that the XP1000 takes memory 4 DIMMS per bank. My spare
Alpha PWS memory might well work but only with the addition of 2 more
DIMMs. The definitive answer from Jay Vlack at HP Support:

> The XP1000 takes buffered JEDEC 21-C and PC100 standard SDRAM DIMM
> memory. The DIMMs must be installed four at a time (one array), and each
> DIMM in an array must be identical. Array0 consists of slots J5 through
> J8, and Array1 consists of slots J1 through J4. Only DIMMs qualified by
> Compaq/HP are guaranteed to work.

thanks,

 john

