"tip" summary,

Added the following line to the "/etc/remote" file;

raid:dv=3D/dev/tty01:br#38400

This meaning COM1 at a baur rate (br) of 38400.


Created the ".tiprc" file in my home directory to ease my exit from tip.
It contains 2 lines;

eol=3Dm
es=3D,

This was necessary because the interface to the external RAID box uses a
lot of escape sequences and this causes problems when exiting "tip".
Now all I have to do is enter; "m,." to exit.

EXECUTION...

"tip raid"

TERMINATION...

"m,."


SEYON Summary

There is an archive out there with the sources still available from
previous versions of (OSF/1(?), DU, and Tru64) if you need them. (Thanks
to Bob Marcan)

http://www.aster.si/download/tru64/SRPMS/seyon-2.14d-1.src.rpm


I currently favor the "tip" solution but it is nice to know that SEYON
is still an option (at least source wise).

